NNAAMMEE
     uuccyyccoomm — device driver for Cypress CY7C63743 and CY7C64013 USB to RS232
     bridges

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following line in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee uussbb
           ddeevviiccee hhiidd
           ddeevviiccee uuccoomm
           ddeevviiccee uuccyyccoomm

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           ucycom_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The uuccyyccoomm driver provides support for the Cypress CY7C63743 and
     CY7C64013 bridge chips.  These chips were designed to provide a low-cost
     transition path to USB for existing RS232 devices, and have fairly lim‐
     ited capabilities.

     The uuccyyccoomm driver behaves like a tty(4).

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The uuccyyccoomm driver currently supports the following devices which incorpo‐
     rate Cypress USB to RS232 bridge chips:

     ••   DeLorme Earthmate USB GPS receiver

FFIILLEESS
     /dev/ttyU*       for callin ports
     /dev/ttyU*.init
     /dev/ttyU*.lock  corresponding callin initial-state and lock-state de‐
                      vices

     /dev/cuaU*       for callout ports
     /dev/cuaU*.init
     /dev/cuaU*.lock  corresponding callout initial-state and lock-state de‐
                      vices

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     tty(4), ucom(4), usb(4)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The uuccyyccoomm driver first appeared in FreeBSD 5.3.

